有 1,300 年历史的稀有衣物碎片</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/archaeologists-in-denmark-discover-rare-fragments-of-1300-year-old-clothing-preserved-inside-viking-age-grave-180989419/</link><description>研究人员在一对金属胸针上发现了织物痕迹。当配件腐蚀时，它们会释放出金属盐，无意中使织物保存了几个世纪</description><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 14:52:27 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/archaeologists-in-denmark-discover-rare-fragments-of-1300-year-old-clothing-preserved-inside-viking-age-grave-180989419/</guid></item><item><title>来认识一下新发现的毛茸茸的鱼种，以《芝麻街》中的 Snuffleupagus 先生命名</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/meet-the-newly-discovered-fuzzy-fish-species-named-after-mr-snuffleupagus-from-sesame-street-180988774/</link><description>鬼海龙邋遢的外表可能使它看起来像漂浮的藻类，使其能够融入环境。自二十多年前首次发现这种奇怪的生物以来，研究人员多年来一直在寻找这种奇怪的生物</description><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/meet-the-newly-discovered-fuzzy-fish-species-named-after-mr-snuffleupagus-from-sesame-street-180988774/</guid></item><item><title>美国宇航局南希·格雷斯·罗马太空望远镜发射寻找系外行星并解开暗物质和暗能量之谜</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/nasas-nancy-grace-roman-space-telescope-launches-to-find-exoplanets-and-unravel-mysteries-of-dark-matter-and-dark-energy-180989268/</link><description>新天文台将在五年内完成三项宇宙调查，尽管它的设计运行时间至少是原来的两倍。它的数据可能会改变科学家对宇宙的基本理解</description><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 11:26:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/nasas-nancy-grace-roman-space-telescope-launches-to-find-exoplanets-and-unravel-mysteries-of-dark-matter-and-dark-energy-180989268/</guid></item><item><title>森林在古代全球变暖事件中表现不佳，为当今的气候变化提供了一个“警示”故事</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/forests-didnt-fare-well-during-an-ancient-global-warming-event-offering-a-cautionary-tale-about-todays-climate-change-180989353/</link><description>一项研究表明，5600 万年前的一场剧烈的全球变暖事件导致现代怀俄明州的森林失去了约 60% 的树冠覆盖率，并且花了 10 万多年的时间才恢复过来</description><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 18:43:58 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/forests-didnt-fare-well-during-an-ancient-global-warming-event-offering-a-cautionary-tale-about-todays-climate-change-180989353/</guid></item><item><title>在西班牙洞穴深处，罗马妇女可能崇拜一位神秘的女神</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/deep-inside-spanish-cave-roman-women-may-have-worshipped-mysterious-goddess-180989414/</link><description>瓦伦西亚的科瓦德莱多内斯 (Cova de les Dones) 以其旧石器时代艺术而闻名，这里还拥有一座罗马圣所，研究人员称，那里的女性似乎在崇拜女性神的过程中发挥了积极作用</description><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 18:43:43 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/deep-inside-spanish-cave-roman-women-may-have-worshipped-mysterious-goddess-180989414/</guid></item><item><title>研究表明，历史污染，而不是当前的工业排放，损害了世界上最大、最古老的古代岩石艺术收藏</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/historical-pollution-not-current-industrial-emissions-damaged-worlds-largest-oldest-collection-ancient-rock-art-180989416/</link><description>研究人员表示，过去接触二氧化硫可能是恩加达-恩加利人数万年前创造的穆鲁朱加岩画孔隙度增加的原因</description><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 18:04:36 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/historical-pollution-not-current-industrial-emissions-damaged-worlds-largest-oldest-collection-ancient-rock-art-180989416/</guid></item><item><title>这颗恒星以破纪录的速度绕我们银河系的中心运行，可能有助于揭开有关那里巨大黑洞的秘密</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-star-orbits-our-galaxys-heart-at-a-record-breaking-speed-and-could-help-uncover-secrets-about-the-behemoth-black-hole-there-180989393/</link><description>Speedster 的行驶速度高达每小时 5600 万英里，约为光速的 8%。它还非常接近银河系中心的超大质量黑洞</description><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 15:45:08 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-star-orbits-our-galaxys-heart-at-a-record-breaking-speed-and-could-help-uncover-secrets-about-the-behemoth-black-hole-there-180989393/</guid></item></channel></rss>